    <name>
      <text>Solving Trigonometric Equations Using Tangent</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Consider the trigonometric equation \(\tan\theta=\sqrt{3}\)</p>

<p><strong>(a)</strong> Determine the reference angle for the given equation.</p>

<p>[[input:ans0]]</p>
<p>[[validation:ans0]]</p>

<p><strong>(b)</strong> Identify the quadrants in which the tangent ratio is positive.</p>

<p>[[input:ans_ref]]</p>
<p>[[validation:ans_ref]]</p>

<p><strong>(c)</strong> Hence, solve the equation for
\(0^\circ\leq\theta<360^\circ\).</p>

<p>First solution:</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]]</p>
<p>[[validation:ans1]]</p>

<p>Second solution:</p>
<p>[[input:ans2]]</p>
<p>[[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p><strong>Instructions:</strong> Give all answers in degrees.</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>

<p>Given the trigonometric equation \(\tan\theta=\sqrt{3}\)</p>
<p><strong>Step 1: Determine the reference angle.</strong></p>

<p>Recall the standard trigonometric value:</p>

\(\tan 60^\circ=\sqrt{3}\)

<p>Therefore, the reference angle is:</p>

\(\alpha=60^\circ\)

<p><strong>Step 2: Identify the quadrants.</strong></p>

<p>The tangent ratio is positive in quadrants I and III.</p>

<p>This means that the solutions must lie in these two quadrants.</p>

<p><strong>Step 3: Determine the first solution.</strong></p>

<p>In quadrant I, the angle is equal to the reference angle:</p>

\(\theta_1=60^\circ\)

<p><strong>Step 4: Determine the second solution.</strong></p>

<p>In quadrant III, add the reference angle to \(180^\circ\):</p>

\(\theta_2=180^\circ+60^\circ=240^\circ\)

<p><strong>Final Answer:</strong></p>

<p>Therefore, the two solutions in the interval
\(0^\circ\leq\theta<360^\circ\) are:</p>

\(\boxed{\theta=60^\circ,\ 240^\circ}\)

<p>Remember that tangent is positive in quadrants I and III, which is why there are two solutions in the given interval.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
